# Skillhouse — Cursor & Agent Design System Rules

## Priority: Mandatory. Overrides default implementation behaviour.

Before creating, modifying, or implementing any UI, you MUST inspect the existing design system and reuse its established components, tokens, patterns, and conventions.

**Never create a new component, style, token, variant, or interaction pattern before verifying that an existing solution cannot meet the requirement.**

1. Inspect Before Implementing:
   - Check `DESIGN_SYSTEM.md` and `:root` variables in `src/app/globals.css`.
   - Inspect primitives in `src/components/primitives/` (`Button`, `Card`, `Input`).
   - Inspect UI elements in `src/components/ui/` (`Checkbox`, `Pill`, `SearchInput`, `FigmaIcon`, `Overlay`).
   - Icons: Strictly enforce `lucide-react` across all components, controls, badges, and interactive elements. Avoid raw SVG icon assets or alternate libraries.
   - Inspect features in `src/components/features/`.
2. Reuse is the default:
   - Tokens: `--color-brand: #FB6320`, `--font-pixel`, `--font-sans`, `--font-mono`.
   - Geometry: 0px radius on buttons/cards/inputs; 4px on checkboxes; circular on avatars/badges.
   - Max-width: 1600px with 40px desktop padding.
3. Build order:
   Tokens -> Primitives -> Reusable Components -> Composite Components -> Sections -> Screens -> Validation.
4. Validation:
   Run `npm run gauntlet` before finishing. Zero lint, type, or test regressions.
